## Scaffolding and documentation plan

Since you don’t want to build yet, you can focus on designing the conceptual skeleton inside your repo.

- Step 1: Clarify the architecture in docs  
  - Update MANIFEST_REVISED.md to describe the multi-layer architecture (perception, routing, brains, orchestration, memory).  
  - Add a diagram (even ASCII) to show how a decision flows through brains and leader profiles.

- Step 2: Define brain and leader schemas  
  - In GLOSSARY.md, introduce terms: “Brain”, “Leader Profile”, “World-Model State”, “Decision Episode”, “Audit Trail”.  
  - In new files (e.g., DEV_BRAIN_SPEC.md, BUSINESS_BRAIN_SPEC.md, etc.), specify the schema for each brain’s inputs, outputs, and internal leader profiles.

- Step 3: Formalize audit and governance  
  - Expand DEV_BRAIN_AUDIT_PROTOCOL.md to cover multi-brain decisions, risk tiers, and human sign-off patterns.  
  - Keep AUDIT_SIGN_OFF.md as the canonical checklist humans use when reviewing high‑risk decisions.

- Step 4: Decision patterns library  
  - Create a DECISION_PATTERNS.md capturing recurring scenarios and which brains and leaders they invoke.  
  - For each pattern, document: typical inputs, success criteria, failure modes, and example questions.

- Step 5: Roadmap (without implementation)  
  - Outline phases like “Prototype in plain English prompts”, “Add simple rule-based layer”, “Introduce data sources,” but keep them high-level.  
  - This will make it easier to move into building mode later without rethinking the entire concept.

